#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""brokenmoon - a tile-based barbarian adventure in the ruins of the Atlantic
seaboard, in Python with Tk or Kivy.

Standard library only (Kivy if you ask for it).  The engine is Dead Drop's
(one hero, a map of squares, people to talk to by keyword, shops, places
below, landmarks painted across several squares), and the rules are The
Black Hack's: six stats rolled 2d6+5, a d20 rolled under a stat for
everything that might fail, foes who never roll to hit (you roll to get
out of the way), damage by Hit Dice, armor that soaks it, usage dice for
everything that runs out, and an Out of Action table instead of death,
mostly.

Ages ago the Moon broke.  Its pieces still hang in the sky, and some of
them fell: sorcery came down with the moonstone, and the old cities of the
coast went to ruin and weeds.  Malgorath the Gilded, the Sorcerer-King,
rules from the cracked dome of the Capitol in Washington.  When the Red
Shard rises full, on the night of the twenty-first day, he will use it to
make a slave of every living thing between the mountains and the sea.  His
door is sealed by a Moon Ward that only three Moonstones open, and his
three warlords hold them, under New York, Boston and Baltimore.

You start in the Free Hold of Philadelphia, by the cracked bell.

Classes: Barbarian, Beastman, Scavenger, Robot, Death Priest, Sorcerer,
Urchin and Raptor, each with its own hit die, damage die, weapons, armor
and tricks.  You go up a level for every Moonstone, and for freeing the
slave pens.

Keys: arrows or WASD move (walk into foes to fight them, people to talk,
doors to go in), Space waits, Z rests an hour, E searches, F fires, C
casts (spells or miracles), U uses or wields something, I your hero, J the
journal, M the map, ? help.

Kivy:                brokenmoon --kivy   (or BROKENMOON_UI=kivy) plays it in
                     a Kivy window; a Python without Tk uses Kivy by itself
Android app:         brokenmoon --build-android [DIR]   a folder
                     (brokenmoon-android/ by default) for Buildozer
App bundle (macOS):  brokenmoon --build-app [DIR]   builds brokenmoon.app
                     brokenmoon --icon-png SIZE [OUT.png]

The tiles are drawn by the code below: no image files.  brokenmoon
--selftest builds every map, room, level and tune without a window.

The rules are adapted from The Black Hack's Open Game Content, as used by
Barbarians of the Ruined Earth (Mike Evans, DIY RPG Productions); the
names, places and story here are this game's own.
"""

